        <item>
            <title>0.1.10</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:31:10 -0600</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>15</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.10</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## What's new in Aretas 0.1.10

*2026-08-13*

The work finished after the last update is finally in the app you are running — the Connections settings, the workspace tree under Tasks, and sending a task where it needs to go.

- Settings now has a Connections tab: each service Aretas can talk to has its own place to sign in, and anything your workplace manages asks your permission first.
- The Tasks section now shows your workspaces as a tree, so you can see where a task would go before you send it.
- Sending a task out shows you exactly what will leave your Mac, and asks you to confirm, before anything is shared.
- If a meeting transcription gets stuck, a problem report now includes that on its own, so you do not have to describe it.
- The Messages and call history switches stay available even when Aretas cannot open your mail — trouble with one source no longer hides the others.
- Review no longer sits waiting when nothing is running. It opens, and says plainly what has and has not been read.
- Topic results and who-told-you answers can now be saved as a PDF or a Word file, or sent to your Drive, the same as the other two reports.
- Correcting an earlier note: when you decide two records are the same, that decision is recorded and Aretas will fold them together in a later update. Nothing has been folded yet.
]]></description>
